{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791242847,"nonce":"dP91Po0Vrfz8vQr0JkPYufhTMSc=","title":"An Int cast to Dynamic stays a raw int, so arithmetic on it is pointer arithmetic (Issue3214)","message":"private abstract Int64_t(Dynamic) { public function get() return this; }\n    // inside an abstract over Int64_t:\n    return new Int64(cast a + b);                         // a, b : Int\n    return new Int64(cast this.get() * a.get().get());\n\nMIR for `cast a + b`:\n\n    $2 = cast i32 $0 to *void\n    $3 = add $2, $1\n\n`cast a` to Dynamic does not box, `+` on a Dynamic operand adds the raw bits, and the product is a raw 21 in a Dynamic slot. `trace(c.get().get())` prints `null`, and `eq(21, c.get().get())` in the row crashes reading the raw value as a box.\n\nReproduces at HEAD with the abstract renamed (MyInt64), so it is independent of the Int64 name collision (451a8a3). Probes: nuc ~/probes/p3214c (as written) and p3214d (renamed). Related: 9744eba (raw scalar dereferenced as a Dynamic box).","files":null}]}